  "full_response": "To create a Kubernetes Secret manifest in YAML with base64-encoded values, you first need to encode your secret values. Below are the steps and the manifest for encoding and decoding you mentioned.\n\n### Secret Values to Encode\n\n1. `db-password`: `superSecretPassword`\n2. `api-key`: `1234567890abcdef`\n3. `tls-cert`: \n   ```\n   -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\n   MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEApBniYrUE1nKoeOysYkB\n   ...\n   -----END CERTIFICATE-----\n   ```\n4. `oauth-client-secret`: `5b4672823b6f9d6b3a097a3d465e1f2c`\n\n### Encoding in Base64\n\nYou can encode these using a command-line tool like `base64`. Here's how to encode them:\n\n```sh\necho -n 'superSecretPassword' | base64\necho -n '1234567890abcdef' | base64\necho -n '-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\nMIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEApBniYrUE1nKoeOysYkB\n...\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----' | base64\necho -n '5b4672823b6f9d6b3a097a3d465e1f2c' | base64\n```\n\n### Example Base64 Encoded Values\n\n1. `db-password`: `c3VwZXJTZWNyZXRQYXNzd29yZA==`\n2. `api-key`: `MTIzNDU2Nzg5MGI2ZjRiOTZhMDk3YTNkM2EwOTZlM2M=`\n3. `tls-cert`: \n   ```\n   LS0tLS1CRUdJTiBDRVJUSUZJQ0FURS0tLS0tCk1JSURzd0lCQURBTkJna3Foa2lHOXcwQkFRc0ZBREFWTVI4d0xUQWVGdzBCQVFzRkFEQXpNUTh3TURBd0NnWURWUVFEREJVeExYQnVib",
